  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 32,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.806,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Which is larger? Find out without fully computing the product."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.112,
            0.422,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 4 \\times 2 6 \\; \\mathrm { o r } \\; 1 6 \\times 2 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.136,
            0.422,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 5 \\times 7 5 \\; \\mathrm { o r } \\; 2 6 \\times 7 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.164,
            0.205,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.183,
            0.519,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 14 \\times 26   and   b = 16 \\times 24"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.201,
            0.607,
            0.28
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_32_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Now} a &= (16 - 2) (24 + 2) \\\\&= 16 \\times 24 + 16 \\times 2 - 2 \\times 24 - 2 \\times 2 \\\\&= b + (32 - 48 - 4) \\\\&= b - 20\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.282,
            0.54,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b > a \\mathrm{~or~} 16 \\times 24 > 14 \\times 26"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.309,
            0.527,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 25 \\times 75   and   b = 26 \\times 74"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.329,
            0.663,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = (26 - 1)(74 + 1) = 26 \\times 74 + 26 - 74 - 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " = b – 49"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.369,
            0.533,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence b > a or 26 × 74 > 25 × 75"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.398,
            0.569,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. A tiny park is coming up in Dhauli. The plan is shown in the figure. The two square plots, each of area "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sq. ft., will have a green cover. All the remaining area is a walking path w ft. wide that needs to be tiled. Write an expression for the area that needs to be tiled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.578,
            0.403,
            0.856,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.578,
                0.403,
                0.856,
                0.509
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_32_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.535,
            0.801,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Length of rectangular park "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w+g+2w+g+w=(2g+4w)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.561,
            0.715,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Breadth of rectangular park "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w + w + g = (g + 2w)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.582,
            0.575,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{park} = (2g + 4w)(g + 2w) \\mathrm{~sq.~ft.}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.601,
            0.556,
            0.622
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_32_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "= 2 g ^ { 2 } + 8 w ^ { 2 } + 8 w g \\mathrm { s q . } \\mathrm { f t } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.627,
            0.55,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the two "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{squares} = 2g^2 \\mathrm{sq}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.651,
            0.628,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, Area to be tiled "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(2g+4w)(g+2w)-2g^{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= 8 w ( w + g ) \\mathrm { s q . f t . }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.702,
            0.499,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. For each pattern shown below,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.726,
            0.615,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Draw the next figure in the sequence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.75,
            0.671,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) How many basic units are there in Step 10?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.774,
            0.847,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Write an expression to describe the number of basic units in"
            }
